# Plan mode's carry-out card returns to the mode worked in before planning,
# not to the modes Shift+Tab passes through on the way. The mock model's
# task runs in `configured`; a message is then sent in `all`, Shift+Tab goes
# on through `ask` to `plan`, and the card offers `all`, with accepting edits
# as a row of its own.
mock-llm
start
wait "README.md"
key Alt+A
wait "Agent"
key Alt+Home Alt+F11
type "flag critical low-stock items in the reorder report"
key Enter
wait "Agent wants to run shell" 20
type "1"
wait "Want me to highlight critical rows" 30
wait-gone "[■]" 15
# configured → auto → all, and work there.
key Shift+Tab Shift+Tab
type "thanks"
key Enter
wait-gone "[■]" 15
# all → ask → plan: passed through, not worked in.
key Shift+Tab Shift+Tab
type "plan highlighting the critical rows"
key Enter
wait "Plan mode: carry the plan out?" 30
expect "Yes, in all mode, from a clean context"
expect "Yes, in all mode"
expect "Yes, accepting edits"
expect-not "Yes, in ask mode"
snapshot card
type "2"
wait-gone "Plan mode: carry the plan out?" 10
wait-gone "[■]" 15
expect "Permissions: all"
snapshot carried
quit
